.TH JSON_COMPACT_PRINTER 3 "JSON Utility" "LIBJSON" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
json_compact_printer - Initialize a compact JSON printer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <lib/json/json.h>
.PP
.B void json_compact_printer(jsonfmt* p, jsonval* v, int depth, int index, char quote);
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B json_compact_printer
function initializes a JSON printer
.IR p
with compact formatting options. The printer will not use indentation, newlines, or spacing between elements.
The printer will use the specified
.IR quote
character for string values.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I p
A pointer to a
.B jsonfmt
structure to be initialized.
.TP
.I v
A pointer to a
.B jsonval
structure to be formatted.
.TP
.I depth
The depth of the current element in the JSON object.
.TP
.I index
The index of the current element in the JSON array.
.TP
.I quote
The quote character to use for string values.
.SH EXAMPLE
The following example demonstrates how to use the
.B json_compact_printer
function:
.PP
.B #include <lib/json/json.h>
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.B int main() {
.B \tjsonval val = ...;
.B \tjsonfmt p;
.B \tjson_compact_printer(&p, &val, 0, 0, '"');
.B \tjson_print(&p, &val);
.B \treturn 0;
.B }
.SH SEE ALSO
.B json_init,
.B json_free